# Review routing for proofhouse-rust-lib. GitHub applies the last
# matching rule, so the supply-chain rules below override the default
# for the paths they name. Owners are org teams (sole member @tbhb for
# now) created with push access, the minimum GitHub requires for a team
# to count as a code owner.

# Default owner for everything.
*             @proofhouse/maintainers

# Supply-chain and CI surface. The /.github/ rule already covers
# renovate.json5 and every workflow, so neither needs its own line. The
# Cargo.toml rule is unanchored on purpose: the workspace resolves one
# lock file from every member manifest, so xtask/Cargo.toml routes here
# alongside the root one.
/.github/     @proofhouse/security
Cargo.toml    @proofhouse/security
/Cargo.lock   @proofhouse/security

# Release-pipeline ownership (@proofhouse/release-engineering) lands
# with the release workflow. That file does not exist yet, so a rule
# here would point at nothing and fail the path-existence gate; it
# arrives alongside the release pipeline.
